<Base title="Affiliate disclosure | WhichPadel" description="How WhichPadel makes money and how affiliate links work."><article class="panel prose">
<h1>Affiliate disclosure</h1><p class="muted">Last updated: 20 October 2026</p>
<p>WhichPadel (https://whichpadel.com) is an independent padel racket comparison site. We are not owned by, or paid to promote, any racket brand.</p>
<h2>How we make money</h2>
<p>Some links on this site, including every "Check price" button, may be <b>affiliate links</b>. If you click one and buy something, the shop may pay us a commission. You pay the same price. Where a link is commercial we label it with "Ad" next to the button, in line with the UK Advertising Standards Authority (CAP Code) and the Competition and Markets Authority's guidance that marketing must be obviously identifiable.</p>
<p>We may also show clearly labelled sponsored placements or newsletter sponsors. These will always be marked "Sponsored" or "Ad".</p>
<h2>What commission never changes</h2>
<ul><li>Ratings are calculated from manufacturers' and retailers' published specifications using our published formula. A commission cannot change them.</li>
<li>Every "best" list states its ranking rule. Rackets are not included, removed or reordered because of payment.</li>
<li>We do not write or publish fake reviews, and we do not claim to have play-tested rackets we have not.</li></ul>
<h2>Prices</h2><p>Prices are snapshots with the date we checked them, not live quotes. Some are converted from euros to pounds at a stated exchange rate and are estimates. Always check the final price, delivery and returns on the shop's site.</p>
<h2>Contact</h2><p>Questions about this policy: [contact email to be added before launch].</p>
</article></Base>
